WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.890
An equation is a balance.

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.050
Take three from both sides and it stays level.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.170
Addition takes us back to the original.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.710
Halve both sides and it still balances.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.550
Doubling takes us back.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.970
A move you can undo keeps exactly the same solutions.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.610
Guessing may find an answer.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.920
Reversible moves let you solve the equation step by step

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.810
and confirm you have kept all of its possible answers.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.030
Two pouches and five counters balance one pouch

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.280
and twelve counters.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.640
Every pouch holds the same number.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.520
How many counters are in a pouch?

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.750
Pause and think about what you could remove

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.900
from both sides.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.770
Remove one pouch from each side.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:43.950
The balance holds.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.430
Now one pouch and five counters balance twelve counters.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.580
Remove five counters from each side.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.900
One pouch balances seven counters.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.660
Each pouch holds seven.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.610
Check in the original.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.990
Two sevens and five make nineteen.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.750
One seven and twelve make nineteen.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.230
Both sides agree.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:07.120
With fractions, clear them by multiplying both sides.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.500
Half a number plus three is eleven.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.040
Take three from both sides: half the number is eight.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.280
Double both sides: the number is sixteen.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.280
One caution.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.630
Before dividing by an unknown number, check whether it

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.320
could be zero.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.950
If a number times itself equals five times the number

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:29.000
and the number is not zero, dividing gives five.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:32.450
Zero also works, because zero times zero equals

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.760
five times zero.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.100
Those two cases cover all possibilities.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.730
Do the same to both sides.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:40.970
Undo one operation at a time.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.450
Check your answer in the original equation.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.860
Notebook challenge: three pouches and four counters

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.370
balance one pouch and eighteen counters.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.810
How many counters are in each pouch?
